Effect-record hook 3: the threaded currently-resolving-sub-ability pointer.

An ability's effect is a chain of sub-abilities: draw a card, then discard one,
then put a counter. Attributing all three outcomes to the root line is coarse
enough to hide which clause did what — and "put a counter" and "draw a card" are
exactly the distinction the per-entity head is being taught.

This hook threads a pointer to the sub-ability currently resolving, so an event
arriving during resolution can name the clause that produced it. The sidecar
records each trait's sub-ability index paths, and an event attributed to a link
the sidecar does not map falls back to the root line rather than being dropped —
so attribution is finer where the pointer is available and never lossy where it
is not.

Per-thread, and restored in a `finally`, because a sub-ability can itself
resolve another.

--- a/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/ability/AbilityUtils.java
+++ b/forge-game/src/main/java/forge/game/ability/AbilityUtils.java
@@ -70,6 +70,27 @@ public class AbilityUtils {

+    // ── effect-record instrumentation (price-predictor spec 023) ──────────
+    //
+    // The sub-ability currently resolving on this thread, or null at the root.
+    // Read by effect-record collection to attribute an outcome to the clause
+    // that produced it rather than to the whole line.
+    private static final ThreadLocal<SpellAbility> EFFECT_RECORD_SUB_ABILITY =
+            new ThreadLocal<>();
+
+    /** The sub-ability currently resolving on this thread, or null. */
+    public static SpellAbility getEffectRecordSubAbility() {
+        return EFFECT_RECORD_SUB_ABILITY.get();
+    }
+
+    private static void setEffectRecordSubAbility(final SpellAbility sa) {
+        if (sa == null) {
+            EFFECT_RECORD_SUB_ABILITY.remove();
+        } else {
+            EFFECT_RECORD_SUB_ABILITY.set(sa);
+        }
+    }
+
     public static void resolve(final SpellAbility sa) {
-        resolveApiAbility(sa, sa.getActivatingPlayer().getGame());
+        final SpellAbility previous = EFFECT_RECORD_SUB_ABILITY.get();
+        setEffectRecordSubAbility(sa);
+        try {
+            resolveApiAbility(sa, sa.getActivatingPlayer().getGame());
+        } finally {
+            // Restored rather than cleared: a sub-ability can resolve another,
+            // and clearing would lose the enclosing clause on the way back up.
+            setEffectRecordSubAbility(previous);
+        }
     }
